WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:53.800
<b>Sandy Island
(The Kingdom of Alabasta)</b>

3
00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:58.220
<b>Sir Crocodile, the Pirate</b>

4
00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:06.730
<b>The Port Town of Nanohana</b>

5
00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:16.320
Sir Crocodile...

6
00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:18.160
Crocodile!

7
00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:19.290
Huh?

8
00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:22.660
Sir Crocodile!

9
00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:24.000
I knew he'd come!

10
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.830
Crocodile?!

11
00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.500
From the Seven Warlords...?

12
00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:31.210
Silence, you fools!

13
00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:35.470
I've only come for that pirate's head!

14
00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:37.300
He's amazing...

15
00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:40.430
He always says that
but saves us anyway!

16
00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:42.350
Hurray for Crocodile!

17
00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:48.230
Alabasta's guardian deity!

18
00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:50.190
Crocodile!

19
00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:53.320
King of the desert! Crocodile!

20
00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:58.490
<b>Sir Crocodile
One of the Seven Warlords of the Sea
Former Bounty: 81 Million Berries</b>

21
00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.830
Well, call me what you will.

22
00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:03.500
Don't just think you can waltz in
and plunder this country, pirates.

23
00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:07.460
Hey, hey, hey, hey!
Aren't you underestimating us?

24
00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:10.460
You thinking of taking us
all on by yourself?!

25
00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:14.130
You sold out to the authorities,
you government dog!

26
00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:16.340
You think you're some kinda hero?!

27
00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:19.300
Those who wish to live,
lay on the ground.

28
00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:22.270
Is he stupid?! He's wide open!

29
00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:26.730
Get him! He won't keep us
from this town's money and valuables!

30
00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:28.480
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

31
00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:37.240
Is this really a famous Warlord?!

32
00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:17.900
I'm a whole different
caliber of pirate, swine.

33
00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.290
Crocodile!

34
00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:59.450
– Crocodile! Crocodile! Crocodile!
– Crocodile! Crocodile! Crocodile!

35
00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:02.910
Crocodile again...

36
00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:05.910
<b>Alubarna Palace
Kingdom of Alabasta</b>

37
00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:05.910
He was one step ahead again?

38
00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:09.750
By the time we got to Nanohana,
it was all over.

39
00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:11.290
I see.

40
00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:14.630
Either way, it's fine
as long as the citizens are safe.

41
00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:18.630
<b>Nefertari Cobra
King of Alabasta</b>

42
00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:18.630
We are indebted to him.

43
00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:22.300
There's no mistake.

44
00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:25.640
Our ship is heading to Alabasta.

45
00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:30.810
Luffy! Don't lie!

46
00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:33.770
Tell me what you know.

47
00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:38.230
Hey, why are you looking away?
Look me in the eyes!

48
00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:43.200
Well... um, really...
I don't know anything.

49
00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:44.870
Then answer me this.

50
00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:50.200
For this trip to Alabasta, I carefully procured
and divided enough food for eight people,

51
00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:52.960
so how did it disappear
during the night?

52
00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:57.710
It's pointless to try and fool me!
You've got the worst poker face.

53
00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:04.840
Hey, you have something
around your mouth.

54
00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:07.310
Shoot! Crumbs?!

55
00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:11.600
It was you!

56
00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:17.440
C'mon...

57
00:06:18.070 --> 00:06:20.570
Oh, Nami... You saw, right?

58
00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:23.530
The large rat trap
just won't do anymore.

59
00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:26.240
Please buy a fridge with a lock.

60
00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:28.450
Well...

61
00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:31.200
I'll think about it...

62
00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:33.660
since our lives may depend on it.

63
00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:40.210
Well then! We'd better
catch something for Sanji.

64
00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:43.220
Hey, any luck fishing?

65
00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:46.470
W-Well...

66
00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:53.980
I feel lucky...

67
00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:56.650
I seriously can't turn
my back for a second!

68
00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:07.370
I'm starving.

69
00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:09.240
The fish aren't biting at all.

70
00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:12.620
Luffy! It's your fault!
I mean, you even ate the bait!

71
00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:14.960
If we don't have bait,
the fish won't bite!

72
00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:16.670
You ate some too!

73
00:07:16.670 --> 00:07:20.000
That's... I only ate what was
stuck to the lid of the bait box.

74
00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:23.510
Luffy. Usopp. Have you
caught anything?

75
00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:29.600
Karoo! Oh, no!

76
00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:32.010
He might catch us a shark.

77
00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:34.810
I wanna catch a sea king.

78
00:07:34.810 --> 00:07:38.480
Just what do you two think
you're doing to Karoo?!

79
00:07:45.530 --> 00:07:46.780
What's that?

80
00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:52.490
What the heck is that?

81
00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:53.790
Maybe it's cotton candy.

82
00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:56.000
I'll go get Nami!

83
00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:03.840
Nami, it's urgent! Come see!

84
00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:11.930
Oh, don't worry.
It's nothing. It's just steam.

85
00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:14.430
Steam is coming up from the sea?

86
00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:15.890
Yeah. It's a hot spot.

87
00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:17.440
What the heck is that?

88
00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:19.850
It's an area where magma spews.

89
00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:22.570
There's an undersea volcano
below that area.

90
00:08:22.570 --> 00:08:23.360
Oh?

91
00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:25.860
A volcano even though it's undersea?

92
00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:31.780
That's right. There are more volcanoes
under the water than above it.

93
00:08:33.410 --> 00:08:35.290
Who cares? We can't eat it.

94
00:08:35.290 --> 00:08:38.960
With an active volcano here,
a new island will be born

95
00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:41.250
over thousands—
or tens of thousands—of years.

96
00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:43.710
You're so cool, Nami!

97
00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:47.260
Tens of thousands of years...
I wonder if I can live that long.

98
00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:49.720
Nah, humans don't live that long.

99
00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:52.720
Caught anything yet?

100
00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:56.600
Oh, Sanji. I'm hungry.
Cook something.

101
00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:58.730
You guys are hopeless.

102
00:08:58.730 --> 00:09:02.650
I'll go upturn the storage
to see if anything's left.

103
00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:15.620
It reeks of sulfur!

104
00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:17.910
We can't see a thing
with steam everywhere!

105
00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:20.580
Bear with it. We should
be through it soon.

106
00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:24.090
Mr. 2 Bon Kurei!

107
00:09:24.090 --> 00:09:25.250
What is it?!

108
00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:28.380
There's smoke at twelve o'clock!

109
00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:31.180
So what?! Sail right through it!

110
00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:34.140
Yes, sir! Going in!

111
00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:35.550
What's with the fog?

112
00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:36.970
We can't see far!

113
00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:45.980
We got through!

114
00:09:47.150 --> 00:09:49.490
Mr. 2 Bon Kurei is gone!

115
00:09:49.490 --> 00:09:50.900
Check inside!

116
00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:52.530
We can't find him!

117
00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:53.410
Can't be!

118
00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:55.910
Mr. 2 Bon Kurei!

119
00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:07.000
Aw, poop!

120
00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:10.760
This duck came from out of nowhere,
and I jumped to it?!

121
00:10:12.050 --> 00:10:13.220
– Is he a human?
– Dunno...

122
00:10:13.930 --> 00:10:15.180
Huh?!

123
00:10:18.850 --> 00:10:21.730
Help me! Please!

124
00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:24.400
I can't swim! I can't swi–

125
00:10:35.950 --> 00:10:37.950
I thought I'd die...

126
00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:41.500
Well... I'm very swan-swan.

127
00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:45.370
"Bon Kurei"

128
00:10:41.500 --> 00:10:45.370
To think that I was saved
by pirates who are total strangers...

129
00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:48.250
I will never forget your kindness!

130
00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:51.760
Also, may I have
a cup of warm soup?

131
00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:52.760
– Like we have it!
– Like we have it!

132
00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:54.430
We're the ones who are hungry!

133
00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:57.300
Oh! Hey there, you!

134
00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:59.890
Aren't you just the cutest?!

135
00:10:59.890 --> 00:11:02.140
Totally my type!
I could just eat you up!

136
00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:04.600
What a weirdo...

137
00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:06.850
So you can't swim, huh?

138
00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:10.820
That's right. I ate a devil fruit.

139
00:11:10.820 --> 00:11:12.780
Really? What kind of fruit?

140
00:11:13.530 --> 00:11:18.660
Well, well... All we can do now is
wait for my ship to come pick me up.

141
00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:21.120
So perhaps I'll put on a little show.

142
00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:24.580
Behold my power!

143
00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:30.340
What are you...?!

144
00:11:30.340 --> 00:11:33.590
Wait! Wait! Wait!

145
00:11:33.590 --> 00:11:35.930
Didn't I say this would be a "show"?

146
00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:36.880
What?!

147
00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:39.720
Nobody's clowning here!

148
00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:42.560
He's me!

149
00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:44.640
Surprised?! Surprised?! Surprised?!

150
00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:49.230
If I touch my face
with my left hand...

151
00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:50.770
See?! Back to normal!

152
00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:53.610
This is the power
of the Clone-Clone Fruit!

153
00:11:54.110 --> 00:11:55.570
Even his voice...

154
00:11:55.570 --> 00:11:57.570
His body was also the same!

155
00:11:57.950 --> 00:11:59.660
A-Amazing!

156
00:11:59.660 --> 00:12:01.240
There!

157
00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:05.080
Oh! Come to think of it,
I didn't have to knock you down.

158
00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:07.460
Because look...!

159
00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:09.830
All that's needed is

160
00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:12.340
to touch your faces
with my right hand.

161
00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:15.090
As you can see, I can

162
00:12:15.090 --> 00:12:16.630
mimic anyone!

163
00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:18.380
Bodies too!

164
00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:21.550
Ouch!

165
00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:22.470
Stop that!

166
00:12:22.850 --> 00:12:24.560
Hey, are you all right?

167
00:12:24.560 --> 00:12:26.560
Ow, ow, ow...

168
00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:31.310
Oh, my... Unfortunately, that's all
I'm willing to show of my power.

169
00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:34.280
You're the best! Show some more!

170
00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:38.400
Oh... Well... if you insist...
I guess I'll show more!

171
00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:41.120
– Yeah! Show it! Show it!
– Yeah! Show it! Show it!

172
00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:41.120
It's not that exciting.

173
00:12:41.120 --> 00:12:43.620
– We wanna see! We wanna see!
– We wanna see! We wanna see! Well then, I guess I'll show...

174
00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:46.620
Furthermore, I'm equipped
with a memory feature!

175
00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:51.080
Here we go!

176
00:13:00.430 --> 00:13:02.890
Spin! Spin! Spin!

177
00:13:03.350 --> 00:13:04.760
Ridiculous!

178
00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:07.180
Spin! Spin!

179
00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:12.020
So, did you like my special talent?

180
00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:14.730
It's rare for me to show it off.

181
00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:18.360
– Cool!
– Cool!

182
00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:22.160
Nobody's clowning here!
Nobody's clowning here!

183
00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:23.620
Oh, whatever!

184
00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:25.830
That's my ship!

185
00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:27.160
– Amazing! Amazing! He's...
– Amazing! Amazing! He's...

186
00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:28.660
Ciao!

187
00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:35.880
"Bon Kurei"

188
00:13:31.420 --> 00:13:34.920
It's already time to say
goodbye? What a shame.

189
00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:35.880
– What?!
– What?!

190
00:13:36.630 --> 00:13:38.340
Please don't go!

191
00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:40.970
Chin up, and don't be sad!

192
00:13:40.970 --> 00:13:43.340
Every voyage contains
some farewells.

193
00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:45.680
But... never forget this:

194
00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:47.640
Friendship...

195
00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:52.480
has nothing to do with how long
we've known each other.

196
00:13:52.480 --> 00:13:54.440
Don't cry!

197
00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:57.400
Let's meet again!

198
00:13:57.400 --> 00:14:00.030
Now, let's go, boys!

199
00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:02.360
Yes, sir! Mr. 2 Bon Kurei!

200
00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:09.750
Mr. 2?!

201
00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:12.580
So then he's...
Mr. 2 Bon Kurei!

202
00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:15.250
Vivi! You've never seen him?!

203
00:14:15.710 --> 00:14:20.210
No... I've never met
Mr. 2 or the Mr. 1 duo.

204
00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:22.420
I don't know their powers, either.

205
00:14:24.220 --> 00:14:26.180
Though I've heard rumors...

206
00:14:27.140 --> 00:14:28.640
Supposedly, Mr. 2 is...

207
00:14:31.560 --> 00:14:35.150
a lanky ballerina who talks
with an effeminate voice.

208
00:14:35.150 --> 00:14:40.730
He always wears a swan coat
that displays "Bon Kurei" on its back.

209
00:14:42.570 --> 00:14:43.650
– You should've noticed!
– You should've noticed!

210
00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:46.240
What's the matter, Vivi?

211
00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:50.450
Among the faces that he pulled
from his past memories...

212
00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:52.790
from his memory feature...

213
00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:54.920
I saw my father's face...

214
00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:59.920
the face of Alabasta's king,
Nefertari Cobra!

215
00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:04.170
If, for example,
you could mimic a king,

216
00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:07.180
you could get away
with just about anything.

217
00:15:07.180 --> 00:15:09.890
We let a troublesome
guy slip away, huh?

218
00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:12.220
So he was our enemy?

219
00:15:12.770 --> 00:15:16.190
He's one hell of a problem
if he's on the opposing side.

220
00:15:17.190 --> 00:15:20.900
If he realizes that we're his enemies...

221
00:15:20.900 --> 00:15:24.650
If he transforms into one of us
using his memory feature,

222
00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:27.660
we won't be able to trust
our own friends.

223
00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:30.370
You sure?

224
00:15:30.370 --> 00:15:32.120
Listen, Luffy–

225
00:15:32.120 --> 00:15:33.750
Wait. Hold it.

226
00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:36.830
While it's true we might just be
going off Luffy's gut feeling,

227
00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:40.170
I believe he's right to think
we don't need to be scared of him.

228
00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:44.840
It's a stroke of luck
that we met up with him...

229
00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:47.130
because now we'll outsmart him.

230
00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:49.970
Mr. 2 Bon Kurei is...

231
00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:49.390
Un, deux, trois!

232
00:15:49.390 --> 00:15:51.930
What's "four" again?

233
00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:51.930
somehow in a very good mood.

234
00:15:54.310 --> 00:15:56.600
I made some new friends today!

235
00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:06.490
<b>Sea Cat (Sea Monster)
Territory: The Coast of Sandy Island</b>

236
00:16:06.490 --> 00:16:08.610
Something popped up!

237
00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:09.780
A sea cat!

238
00:16:09.780 --> 00:16:12.780
It's a sea monster!

239
00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:16.000
It's our first meal in four days!

240
00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:17.290
It's food!

241
00:16:17.290 --> 00:16:19.370
We're on the right track.

242
00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:22.840
I hope we get there soon.

243
00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:24.670
Food!

244
00:16:26.550 --> 00:16:28.010
Whoa! It's backing away!

245
00:16:28.010 --> 00:16:29.840
Go back! Full reverse!

246
00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:31.760
W-W-W-W-W-W-We can't!

247
00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:33.720
Oh!

248
00:16:34.100 --> 00:16:37.060
Don't let it get away!
We have to capture it!

249
00:16:39.270 --> 00:16:42.400
Now, how would you like
to be cooked, cat monster?!

250
00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:45.360
You can't!

251
00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:51.320
Vivi! You jerk! What are you doing?!

252
00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:53.660
Wh... Why... Vivi?

253
00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:55.410
You can't eat it!

254
00:16:55.830 --> 00:16:59.370
Sea cats are a sacred
animal in Alabasta!

255
00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:00.370
Tell us sooner!

256
00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:03.090
The sea's full of all kinds of creatures!

257
00:17:04.380 --> 00:17:07.090
You've got a ways to go if you're
scared of things like that.

258
00:17:07.090 --> 00:17:08.670
Okay then!

259
00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:13.510
Here's a story all about how I bravely
fought off sea kings in the Calm Belt.

260
00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:15.140
Fought off sea kings?!

261
00:17:15.140 --> 00:17:17.850
Big ones! They were this big!

262
00:17:18.310 --> 00:17:21.310
O-Our food got away...

263
00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:24.860
It will all be okay! You'll soon
have plenty to fill your belly!

264
00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:28.320
Really?! What kind of cat
will appear next time?!

265
00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:32.280
Vivi! The wind and weather
seem to be stabilizing.

266
00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:33.660
Yes.

267
00:17:33.660 --> 00:17:36.160
We've entered
Alabasta's climate area.

268
00:17:36.160 --> 00:17:38.750
A sea cat appearing
is a sure sign, too.

269
00:17:39.160 --> 00:17:41.370
And just look behind us.

270
00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:43.710
More proof Alabasta's
close by, right?

271
00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:57.470
There are so many ships!
When did that happen?!

272
00:17:57.850 --> 00:18:02.440
Hey! They're all flying
Baroque Works' colors!

273
00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:05.900
Its employees have started gathering.

274
00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:10.780
They're most likely the billions,
the officer agents' subordinates.

275
00:18:10.780 --> 00:18:14.030
Then there are at least
200 men out there.

276
00:18:14.030 --> 00:18:17.740
In point of fact, they're
the 200 elites of Baroque Works.

277
00:18:18.290 --> 00:18:21.200
The bounty hunters at
Whisky Peak don't even compare.

278
00:18:22.210 --> 00:18:24.460
Should we fire at them
while we can?!

279
00:18:25.630 --> 00:18:27.880
Let's get the drop on them!

280
00:18:27.880 --> 00:18:30.420
It's quicker if we go
there and beat them up!

281
00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:33.880
No, wait! We gotta eat first!

282
00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:36.850
It'd be dumb to bother
with those small-timers.

283
00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:38.970
He's right.

284
00:18:38.970 --> 00:18:41.810
If we lose sight of our
real target, we're done for.

285
00:18:41.810 --> 00:18:44.270
And there are only eight of us.

286
00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:49.070
Just... tie it tightly.

287
00:18:49.070 --> 00:18:51.230
Our enemy this time
is overly secretive.

288
00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:52.530
Perfect.

289
00:18:52.530 --> 00:18:56.200
These will help us tell
who our real crewmates are.

290
00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:59.200
Does that Clone-Clone Fruit guy...

291
00:18:59.660 --> 00:19:02.620
really become so similar
when he transforms?

292
00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:05.120
Seeing is believing!
It's not just "similar,"

293
00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:06.670
it's identical!

294
00:19:06.670 --> 00:19:11.800
It's too bad! You should've seen it.
We even danced with him.

295
00:19:11.800 --> 00:19:15.220
Knowing someone like that
is among our enemy,

296
00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:17.760
we can't carelessly act alone.

297
00:19:19.890 --> 00:19:22.720
Hey, what should I do?

298
00:19:22.720 --> 00:19:26.810
Well... Do what you can do.
You don't have to do anything more.

299
00:19:26.810 --> 00:19:29.360
It's okay to run away from
an enemy you can't defeat!

300
00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:32.150
Are you talking to him or yourself?

301
00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:35.780
What I can do, huh?

302
00:19:36.280 --> 00:19:37.490
Got it!

303
00:19:37.490 --> 00:19:40.030
I can see the island now!

304
00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:43.450
We'll visit Nanohana, that town ahead,
but we need to hide the ship.

305
00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:47.330
Alright! So, no matter what happens,

306
00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:50.960
our left arms prove
that we're definitely crewmates!

307
00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:56.170
Now, let's get ashore!

308
00:19:56.170 --> 00:19:58.840
To a restaurant!
Oh, and to Alabasta.

309
00:19:59.590 --> 00:20:01.180
– As a side note?
– As a side note?

310
00:20:03.140 --> 00:20:06.890
Our enemy this time is
a group of assassins, Luffy.

311
00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:08.230
Yeah. That's right.

312
00:20:08.230 --> 00:20:11.110
Be careful about acting
on instinct, okay?

313
00:20:11.110 --> 00:20:16.740
You're right. I got it.
Yeah! That's right! Yeah! Got it!

314
00:20:19.490 --> 00:20:22.620
<b>The Port of Nanohana,
The Kingdom of Alabasta</b>

315
00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:32.210
Hey! What's going on?
What happened?

316
00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:36.670
Oh. It seems someone
keeled over in that restaurant.

317
00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:37.670
Keeled over?!

318
00:20:38.590 --> 00:20:42.470
He seems to have died in the middle
of a conversation with the proprietor!

319
00:20:42.470 --> 00:20:44.350
He's an out-of-towner.

320
00:20:44.350 --> 00:20:48.600
We think he unwittingly ate
a desert strawberry while traveling.

321
00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:50.400
A desert strawberry?

322
00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:54.270
They're poisonous spiders that
look like red strawberries.

323
00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:58.700
Eat one by accident, and you'll
suddenly drop dead a few days later.

324
00:20:58.700 --> 00:21:03.240
Contagious poison spreads through
the corpse for a few hours after that,

325
00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:05.830
so nobody can get close.

326
00:21:05.830 --> 00:21:09.660
In the desert, what you
don't know can kill you.

327
00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:15.170
Just look! The way he's stuck
in that position, still holding the meat,

328
00:21:15.170 --> 00:21:19.720
is proof of just how powerful
the desert strawberry's poison is!

329
00:21:24.430 --> 00:21:26.140
He came back to life!

330
00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:34.440
A-Are you all right?

331
00:21:39.780 --> 00:21:41.610
Oh, my bad.

332
00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:42.780
I dozed off.

333
00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:44.910
– That was dozing off?!
– That was dozing off?!

334
00:21:44.910 --> 00:21:48.500
R-Ridiculous! You were in the middle
of a conversation and a meal!

335
00:21:48.500 --> 00:21:50.620
And he's right back to eating!

336
00:21:52.620 --> 00:21:54.580
So what's the big fuss?

337
00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:57.590
– We were worried you'd died!
– We were worried you'd died!

338
00:21:57.590 --> 00:22:00.590
Is this restaurant known
for comedy routines?

339
00:22:00.590 --> 00:22:05.300
No, it's not like that.
But we're glad you're okay.

340
00:22:06.010 --> 00:22:08.060
– Hey! Don't just pass out again!
– Hey! Don't just pass out again!

341
00:22:12.100 --> 00:22:14.270
Huh? So he wasn't really dead?

342
00:22:14.270 --> 00:22:16.230
Just a false alarm.

343
00:22:24.700 --> 00:22:27.240
That hit the spot!

344
00:22:27.240 --> 00:22:28.490
Say, Mister...

345
00:22:28.490 --> 00:22:30.080
Yeah?!

346
00:22:30.080 --> 00:22:32.540
You seen this guy in town?

347
00:22:32.540 --> 00:22:34.710
He's a pirate with a straw hat...

348
00:22:34.710 --> 00:22:38.920
You've got a lot of guts
eating out in public,

349
00:22:39.460 --> 00:22:42.630
Second Division commander
of the Whitebeard Pirates...

350
00:22:43.470 --> 00:22:47.800
<b>Commander Portgas D. Ace
Second Division
Whitebeard Pirates</b>

351
00:22:43.630 --> 00:22:47.800
Portgas D. Ace.

352
00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:51.180
Wh-Whitebeard?!
The Whitebeard Pirates?!

353
00:22:51.770 --> 00:22:54.900
That numbskull is one of
the Whitebeard Pirates?!

354
00:22:54.900 --> 00:22:57.440
You know, I recognize
the tattoo on his back!

355
00:22:57.440 --> 00:23:00.190
That's the mark
of the Whitebeard Pirates!

356
00:23:00.190 --> 00:23:01.690
What's he doing here?!

357
00:23:02.650 --> 00:23:06.660
What's a famous, big-shot pirate
doing in this country?

358
00:23:12.290 --> 00:23:13.750
Just looking...

359
00:23:17.170 --> 00:23:19.170
for my kid brother!
